Sectoare de activitate: Fabricația de utilaje pentru automatizări
HARTING stands for strong connections – across the globe. As one of the leading international suppliers of industrial connectivity, we are connecting customers to their digital future. And as an employer? We connect around 6,000 people at our headquarter in Espelkamp and at locations worldwide. Here you’ll find great colleagues, as well as ever new opportunities and innovations revolving around IoT and artificial intelligence. In everything we do, we remain true to our roots: as a regionally connected family business that always stays firmly grounded in spite of our stellar high-tech. Here’s to your unique future with us: Yours!
 Responsabilities
 Support in monitoring global supply chain activities using various software tools;
 Assist in analyzing data to identify trends, Service Level Performance, Backlog development, forecast demand, and plan inventory levels;
 Help collaborate with customer service, manufacturers, and logistics providers to improve supply chain processes;
 Contribute to developing reports on supply chain performance metrics for management review;
 Assist in identifying and implementing improvements to enhance efficiency and reduce costs;
 Support compliance with international trade regulations and standards;
 Help maintain and ensure the accuracy of data across systems, including customer, vendor, and material data;
 Assist in creating dashboards and reports to support supply chain stakeholders, identifying trends and opportunities for improvement;
 Help visualize KPIs and performance indicators using tools like SAC, Power BI, Celonis, or Excel;
 Collaborate with various departments to ensure smooth data flow and process integration across the supply chain;
 Adapt new data analytic tools and data services.
 Requirements
 Bachelor's degree in a relevant field or comparable specialised training;
 1-5 years of professional experience / industry experience;
 Very good command of written and spoken English (position dependent).
 Benefits: Flexibility (RO), Meal tickets (RO), Medical services (RO), Annual bonus salary (RO), Recreational activities (RO)
